  "notes": "The music room added to an existing house above the Rio de la Plata. From the entrance elevation (gravel forecourt, low exposed-concrete podium with a broad step, a glazed wall between board-formed concrete wall ends, a carved screen beside it, the dark metal-clad roof slab with a wood soffit overhanging all round), the river-side views (deep roof over a covered corner terrace held by a single round column, frameless glass corner, deck running past the roof edge) and the glazed corridor view (a glass link, glass on both sides, running to the existing house). The river is taken as south. Dimensions scaled from the glazing height (~3 m) and a person; the plan of the room, the existing house beyond the link (a dark-framed glass volume and a rendered block) and the low concrete block west of the terrace are estimated. Lavender and native-grass clumps stand in for the planting; the rocks are rough."
